                        <div class="globe-callout" id="dbe-status">
                            <h3>DBE status — the 2025 USDOT rule, stated plainly</h3>
                            <p>Globe Electric Supply holds Texas DBE certification and continues to hold it. The USDOT <strong>Interim Final Rule</strong> (49 CFR Parts 23 &amp; 26, effective 3 October 2025) required a nationwide reevaluation of existing DBE certifications. That rule suspended <em>counting</em> DBE participation toward federal contract goals while reevaluation is incomplete — <strong>it did not revoke any certification.</strong> The same is true of every Texas DBE; the TUCP reevaluation is still in progress and must conclude by <strong>24 December 2026</strong>.</p>
                            <p>Practical effect for a contracting officer: Globe's certification remains in force. Counting toward a federal goal should be confirmed with the TUCP at the time of award. Certification evidence is available on request.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="globe-callout globe-callout-muted">
                            <h3>Not claimed</h3>
                            <p>Globe does <strong>not</strong> hold SDVOSB, ISO certification, or SCTRCA certification. Any document asserting otherwise is not current. This page lists only certifications verifiable in the issuing agency's directory.</p>
                        </div>
