                <section class="globe-section globe-section-white" id="terms">
                    <div class="globe-container">
                        <div class="globe-section-head">
                            <p class="globe-eyebrow">Terms on this page</p>
                            <h2>What the terms mean</h2>
                            <p>Plain definitions of the certifications and identifiers procurement offices ask for.</p>
                        </div>
                        <dl class="globe-terms">
                            <div class="globe-term" id="mbe"><dt><span>MBE</span> Minority Business Enterprise</dt><dd>A business at least 51% owned and controlled by members of a minority group, certified by the issuing agency. Globe is certified by the City of Houston Office of Business Opportunity.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="wbe"><dt><span>WBE</span> Women Business Enterprise</dt><dd>A business at least 51% owned and controlled by women, certified by the issuing agency. Globe is certified by the City of Houston.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="sbe"><dt><span>SBE</span> Small Business Enterprise</dt><dd>A business that meets the certifying agency's size standards. Globe holds SBE certification with the City of Houston, LA Metro, Port Houston and TxDOT.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="dbe"><dt><span>DBE</span> Disadvantaged Business Enterprise</dt><dd>The US Department of Transportation programme under 49 CFR Part 26 for federally assisted transportation contracts. In Texas, DBE certification is issued through the Texas Unified Certification Program.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="naics"><dt><span>NAICS</span> North American Industry Classification System</dt><dd>Six-digit codes that classify what a business does. Solicitations use them to define who may bid.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="nigp"><dt><span>NIGP</span> NIGP Commodity Codes</dt><dd>Codes from the National Institute of Governmental Purchasing that public agencies use to classify what they buy.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="duns"><dt><span>DUNS</span> Data Universal Numbering System</dt><dd>The nine-digit business identifier issued by Dun &amp; Bradstreet, still requested by many agencies and prime contractors.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="uei"><dt><span>UEI</span> Unique Entity ID</dt><dd>The identifier the US federal government uses for entities doing business with it, assigned through SAM.gov.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="cage"><dt><span>CAGE</span> Commercial and Government Entity Code</dt><dd>A five-character identifier for suppliers to the US government, assigned on SAM.gov registration.</dd></div>
                            <div class="globe-term" id="b2g"><dt><span>B2G</span> B2G Vendor ID</dt><dd>The vendor identifier in B2Gnow, the certification and compliance system many agencies use. Globe's B2G Vendor ID is the same across every agency that uses it.</dd></div>
                        </dl>
                    </div>
